.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CMS_ENCRYPTEDDATA_DECRYPT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CMS_EncryptedData_decrypt ,
.Nm CMS_EnvelopedData_decrypt
.Nd Decrypt CMS EncryptedData or EnvelopedData
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_EncryptedData_decrypt
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "const unsigned char *key"
.Fa "size_t keylen"
.Fa "BIO *dcont"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fc
.Ft BIO *
.Fo CMS_EnvelopedData_decrypt
.Fa "CMS_EnvelopedData *env"
.Fa "BIO *detached_data"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fa "ASN1_OCTET_STRING *secret"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CMS_EncryptedData_decrypt
decrypts a
.Fa cms
EncryptedData object using the symmetric
.Fa key
of size
.Fa keylen
bytes.
.Fa out
is a BIO to write the content to and
.Fa flags
is an optional set of flags.
.Fa dcont
is used in the rare case where the encrypted content is detached.
It will normally be set to NULL.
.Pp
The following flags can be passed in the
.Fa flags
parameter.
.Pp
If the
.Sy CMS_TEXT
flag is set MIME headers for type
.Qo Li text/plain Qc
are deleted from the content.
If the content is not of type
.Qo Li text/plain Qc
then an error is returned.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_decrypt
decrypts, similarly to CMS_decrypt(3), a CMS EnvelopedData object
.Fa env
using the symmetric key
.Fa secret
if it is not NULL, otherwise the private key of the recipient
.Fa pkey .
If
.Fa pkey
is given, it is recommended to provide also the associated certificate
in
.Fa cert
- see
.Xr CMS_decrypt 3
and the NOTES on
.Fa cert
there.
The optional parameters
.Fa flags
and
.Fa dcont
are used as described above.
The optional parameters library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq
are used when retrieving algorithms from providers.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn CMS_EncryptedData_decrypt
returns 0 if an error occurred otherwise returns 1.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_decrypt
returns NULL if an error occurred, otherwise a BIO containing the
decypted content.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr CMS_EncryptedData_encrypt 3 ,
.Xr CMS_decrypt 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_decrypt
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
